WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.590
- Alright, before we say goodbye,

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:04.110
I have one more great story to
share on this Veteran's Day.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.516
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.516 --> 00:00:07.184
(upbeat music)

00:00:07.184 --> 00:00:08.808
(cheering)

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.820
This has always been a source
of healing for veterans,

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:12.930
including dance,

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:15.090
And in Florida a retired
veteran switched out

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.373
his combat boots for tap shoes.

00:00:18.331 --> 00:00:20.748
(jazz music)

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.890
(cheering) That's Mack Max,
the veteran known Major Mac.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.560
He's the founder of the Veterans
Art Center in Tampa Bay.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.150
We have him on the line right now watching

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:38.460
on Tampa Bay's MOR-TV.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.359
What's up Major Mac?

00:00:40.359 --> 00:00:41.609
- Hey. Hey, hey.

00:00:41.609 --> 00:00:42.442
What's up?

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.275
(cheering)

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:44.855
What's going on in New York?

00:00:44.855 --> 00:00:46.740
- Oh man, well, how long did it take you

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.480
to learn how to tap?

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.340
- Oh, it took me about five weeks.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.050
Lindsey White, my instructor,

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.540
was my drill sergeant for five weeks.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.600
So, we did a tap dance instruction

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.780
and for our dance party
when Hurricane Ian hit

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.300
at Fred Astaire, we had
this tap dancing theme

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.190
and all of my board members
are like, Major Mac,

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:08.130
Major Mac, can you do a tap dance?

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:10.500
And I said, yeah, anything
to bring in people

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.660
and create memories and laughter.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.920
- Yeah, and it feels good.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.132
I used to tap when I was a kid, it's fun.

00:01:15.132 --> 00:01:15.965
- [Major Mac] Yeah.

00:01:15.965 --> 00:01:17.310
- So this, there's a serious reason

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.360
behind this though, right?

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.330
- Yeah, so I retired out of USF St. Pete

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:22.650
and US Army Cadet Command

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.960
and running in downtown St. Petersburg.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.362
I had this epiphany to start a
center for military veterans,

00:01:28.362 --> 00:01:30.360
first responders and families

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.150
and actually this is our 10th
year anniversary as well.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.660
And so we do mental health
healing and suicide prevention

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.450
and we're up to four
prevented suicides right now.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.200
Currently we reached out
around 2,000, 2,500 veterans

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.960
with our various programs that
we have done and are doing.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.404
- Wow, well thank you so much Major Mac.

00:01:48.404 --> 00:01:49.608
(cheering)

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:52.316
I'm liking your posts right now, right?

00:01:52.316 --> 00:01:53.149
- [Major Mac] Yes.

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:53.982
(dinging)

00:01:53.982 --> 00:01:54.990
- And that's actually not all,

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.540
our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.280
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.980
believe in your efforts
to support veterans.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:02.813
So they're gonna be writing

00:02:02.813 --> 00:02:05.640
the Veterans Art Center of
Tampa Bay a check for $1,000.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:06.473
What's the sound?

00:02:06.473 --> 00:02:09.330
(cheering)

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:10.860
Thank you so much Major Mac

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.750
and thank you to all our guests this hour:

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:17.310
Al Roker, Deborah Roberts,
Matt Rife, Major Sam Winkler,

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.707
Staff Sargent Karen Vargas,
Greg Morgan and Jelly Roll.

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:23.910
And a big thank you to all
the men and women serving

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.727
and sacrificing for our country.

00:02:25.727 --> 00:02:28.170
We salute you, we thank
you, we appreciate you.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:31.593
Have a great day, and if
it's not, try and change it.

